#: ../../.opencode/commands/why.md:4
msgid ""
"Resolve the user's target (a spec slug, an `<spec-slug>:AC-N` criterion "
"id, a file path, or a commit SHA) and walk origin edges in reverse so the"
" chain reads oldest-first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/why.md:8
msgid "If the user named a specific target, run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/why.md:10
msgid "hero why <target>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/why.md:12
msgid ""
"If the target is ambiguous, ask once. Origin edge types walked: "
"`belongs_to`, `satisfied_by`, `attempted_in`, `decided_in`, `supersedes`,"
" `mentions`, `depends_on`, `derived_from`, `originated_in`, `closes`, "
"`fixes`. Default depth is 4 hops; pass `--depth N` to extend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/why.md:18
msgid ""
"The output is a markdown trace. Surface it verbatim to the user; then "
"summarize the throughline in one sentence so the chain is meaningful even"
" if the user skims."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/why.md:22
msgid ""
"For a flat dump of every adjacent edge instead of the recursive trace, "
"use `hero why <target> --edges`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/why.md:25
msgid "$ARGUMENTS"
msgstr ""

